{"title":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","category":"Engineering","bank":"nta_abhyas_jee_main","subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Mathematical Induction","count":3,"questions":[{"id":91243,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Mathematical Induction","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"If <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math> are two distinct integers and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> is a natural number then <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup></math> is divisible by","options":["<math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>","<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math>","<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math>","None of these"],"answer":2,"solution":"<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup></math> where <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math><br /><br />Then, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi> </mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math> is divisible <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> is divisible <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> is divisible <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math><br /><br />Hence <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup></math> is divisible <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main) 2020","_marksId":"6151e8639d8a2183646eaf36"},{"id":91244,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Mathematical Induction","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"If <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>27</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>999</mn></mrow></msup></math> is divided by <math><mn>7,</mn></math> then the remainder is","options":["<math> <mtext>1</mtext></math>","<math> <mtext>2</mtext></math>","<math> <mtext>3</mtext></math>","<math> <mtext>6</mtext> </math>"],"answer":3,"solution":"Express the given number <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mn>27</mn></mrow> <mrow> <mn>999</mn></mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math> as <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced> <mrow> <mn>28</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> </mfenced></mrow> <mrow> <mn>999</mn></mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math><br />Now, divide by <math> <mrow>  <mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></math> <math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow> <mrow> <mn>999</mn></mrow> </msup> </mrow> <mn>7</mn> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br />and apply the formula of binomial expansion.<br />We get the reminder as <math> <mrow> <mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow> </math>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main) 2020","_marksId":"6151e8636aa857b5c06159c1"},{"id":91245,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Mathematical Induction","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"<math><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup><mo><</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>!</mo></math> is true for <math><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>","options":["<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo><</mo><mn>4</mn></math>","<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></math>","<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo><</mo><mn>3</mn></math>","None of these"],"answer":1,"solution":"<math> <mrow> <mtext>P</mtext><mfenced> <mtext>n</mtext> </mfenced><mo> : </mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup><mo><</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>!</mo></math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>P</mtext><mfenced> <mtext>1</mtext> </mfenced><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext>P</mtext><mfenced> <mn>2</mn> </mfenced><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext>P</mtext><mfenced> <mn>3</mn> </mfenced></mrow> </math> are not true.<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>P</mtext><mfenced> <mtext>4</mtext> </mfenced><mo> : </mo></mrow><mn>16</mn><mo><</mo><mn>24</mn></math> is true<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtext>P</mtext><mfenced> <mtext>K</mtext> </mfenced></mrow> </math> : <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>!</mo><mo>></mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow></msup></math> is true for some <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>></mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><br />To prove <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>: </mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>!</mo><mo>></mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is true<br /><br />Multiplying both sides of <math> <mrow> <mtext>P</mtext><mfenced> <mtext>K</mtext> </mfenced></mrow> </math> by <math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>),</mo></math> we get,<br /><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>!</mo><mo>></mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>></mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>></mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br />Hence by <math> <mrow> <mtext>PMI,</mtext></mrow> </math> <math> <mrow> <mtext>P</mtext><mfenced> <mtext>n</mtext> </mfenced></mrow> </math> is true <math><mo>∀</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></math>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main) 2020","_marksId":"6151e863c346cefa5ccf880f"}]}